course: dictionary
lesson: 2091
title: Words that show scorn
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone does something. «She looked at him contemptuously.» The word contemptuously tells you how she looked. Words ending in -ly, like quickly or sadly, often tell you how an action is done.
explain: Use the clues around the word. She looked at him, and the way she looked shows she thinks he is not worth any respect. Ask: would a kind, friendly look fit here? No, so contemptuously must mean with scorn. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
explain: The same kind of word appears in famous stories. In The Wind in the Willows, the weasels and the bargewoman treat Toad contemptuously. In Alice, the Caterpillar asks «Who are you?» contemptuously. In both, the speaker thinks the other person is worthless.
fact: Contemptuously means in a way that shows you think someone or something is worthless or does not deserve respect.
fact: Contemptuously is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «She looked at him contemptuously» means she looked at him as if he did not deserve any respect.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the weasels and the bargewoman treat Toad contemptuously.
fact: Contempt is a strong feeling of looking down on someone, so it is more than just disliking them.
exercise: «She looked at him contemptuously.» What does contemptuously mean? | In a way that shows she is very happy | In a way that makes her laugh | Very slowly and carefully | *In a way that shows she thinks he is not worth respect
exercise: In Alice, the Caterpillar asks «Who are you?» contemptuously. What is he showing? | He is very tired | Fear of the answer | Excitement about meeting Alice | *Scorn, as if Alice is not worth his respect
exercise: Find and copy the adverb in «She looked at him contemptuously.» | she | him | looked | *contemptuously
test: «The rude boy sneered at the little girl contemptuously.» What does contemptuously tell you? | *He thought she was not worth respect | He was running fast | He was feeling very cold | He was laughing at a joke
test: The weasels spoke to Toad contemptuously. What does this show about them? | They respected Toad greatly | They were afraid of Toad | They wanted to make Toad laugh | *They looked down on Toad and thought he was worthless
exam: Which word means nearly the same as contemptuously? | Respectfully | Sleepily | *Scornfully | Kindly
